[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8c77c325-2e41-51df-821c-943abffd054d" "question-9362856b-6dfd-5551-b35f-afef6a56607c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c77c325-2e41-51df-821c-943abffd054d" :question/id #uuid "8c77c325-2e41-51df-821c-943abffd054d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75520" :question/problem "${7.3}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to calculate the product of $7.3$ with itself:\n\n$$\n{7.3}^{2}=(7.3)\\cdot (7.3)\n$$\n\nFirst, we ignore the decimal points and multiply as if both numbers were whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{2} \\\\ \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $73\\times 73=5\\,329.$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in the first factor ($7.3$) and $1$ decimal place in the second factor ($7.3$), so their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nWe take our value of $5\\,329$ and insert a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places:\n\n$$\n53\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{29}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${7.3}^{2}=53.29\\,.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b277ddb-c4ed-5fd4-b2dc-c14fccceaffe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:d